claimed: source-merge-chunked — the question put directly: if Chunks.merge is 10.7us against Source.merge's 299.7us on the same 2x500, why does Source.merge not chunk INTERNALLY and re-tell elementwise, keeping its per-element API? Obstacle: merge is defined by READINESS, and a fixed batch delays an element that is ready now. So measure the CEILING first (fixed chunk, worst-case semantics, benchmark only, no API change) -- if the prize is large, design the adaptive form that only batches when the consumer is already behind; if it is small, the question is closed with a number.
